window.docContents[33].resolve({"/Abstraction/Function-and-program/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Function-and-program":{"contents":"A function is well typed when its body is well typed under the context of its parameters and its result type. Its result type is void or storable, each parameter type is bindable, and every type is well formed. A reference parameter may thus have an object type.\n\nA program is a list of declarations of classes and functions with a function int main(). The initial store is empty, because there are no global variables, and the result is the value of main().Two functions of one name have distinct and distinguishable signatures, . Each class  is well formed,  of . Each class template a header declares has a module of , and each function it declares has one that agrees with the declaration.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Abstraction","header":"5.5. Function and program","id":"/Abstraction/Function-and-program/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Function-and-program"}});